            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 9-year-old boy presented with a 3-month history of cervical pain, limited range of motion, and a palpable &quot;bump&quot; in his posterior neck. After treatment with antibiotics for presumptive adenopathy and progression of the palpable finding, radiographs were obtained.</AbstractText>
